We substitute the expression for $g(x)$ into $f(g(x))$ and $g(f(x))$:
\begin{align*}
f(g(x)) &= f\left(\frac{x}{3} + 2\right) = 6\left(\frac{x}{3} + 2\right) - 9 = 2x + 12 - 9 = 2x + 3, \\
g(f(x)) &= g(6x - 9) = \frac{6x - 9}{3} + 2 = 2x - 3 + 2 = 2x - 1.
\end{align*}
Finally, we subtract $g(f(x))$ from $f(g(x))$:
\begin{align*}
f(g(x)) - g(f(x)) &= (2x + 3) - (2x - 1) \\
&= 2x + 3 - 2x + 1 \\
&= \boxed{4}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 4

