To find the repetend, we perform long division to find the decimal representation of $\frac{3}{13}.$

$$
\begin{array}{c|cccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.} & \multicolumn{1}{|c}{2} & 3 & 0 \\
\cline{2-5}
13 & 3. & 0 & 7 & 6 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{2.} & 6 &  \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 3 & 0 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 2 & 6 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 4 & 0 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 3 & 9 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 1 \\
\end{array}
$$

We can see that the decimal representation of $\frac{3}{13}$ is $0.\overline{230769}.$

